WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.670
In 2023, consumer spending
was 67.5 percent of US GDP.

2
00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:10.450
Add business investment, government
purchases and net exports,

3
00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:12.790
and you get aggregate demand.

4
00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:16.270
Now imagine every price in
the country rises at once,

5
00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:19.350
from groceries to gas to movie tickets.

6
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:23.890
Economists say Americans
would still buy less real GDP.

7
00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.880
So if every price in a
country goes up at once,

8
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.940
why would people buy less
of the country's output?

9
00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.790
In this mission, you'll draw
the aggregate demand curve

10
00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:34.700
and see what it is made of.

11
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:37.220
Then you'll use a graph
lab to separate a move

12
00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:40.490
along the curve from a
shift of the whole curve.

13
00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:43.740
Your mission: explain why
the curve slopes down,

14
00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:44.930
and what moves it.
